re,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{3\\sqrt{14}})≈{11.49}^{∘}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad90516-6de3-5322-9799-56d50aedcba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{104.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284878} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4ce063-2662-501f-a7d4-6cffbba3f19a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110.8}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285201} {:answer/id #uuid "38a6c708-fe56-5283-a85a-91fad1eaa1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{92.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285317} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba26421-66e7-5b20-882a-624c20d91ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{84.7}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285628} {:answer/id #uuid "85ac83f4-5a71-50ed-ae67-c0b78cdc3044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{132.4}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ad90516-6de3-5322-9799-56d50aedcba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{104.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284878} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d084ddf-6dab-583a-a6fe-289d9ce77544" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "024f1eea-1cf9-519a-baef-cf481604490c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19038" :question/problem "Given that $p\\cdot q=-5$, find the angle between $p=⟨4t,-2,t⟩$ and $q=⟨1,3,-3⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $p\\cdot q=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =-5 \\\\ 4t\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 3+t\\cdot (-3) & =-5 \\\\ 4t-6-3t & =-5 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨4(1),-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $p$ and $q$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,||\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{21}\\cdot \\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{399}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTHerefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{399}})≈{104.5}^{∘}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "119553ca-0ce0-58fd-9b51-f2f111158c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60.87}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284942} {:answer/id #uuid "3def5090-4e19-5882-b3c2-a8ec27d56584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54.98}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285373} {:answer/id #uuid "662de5f1-37f4-53e3-941c-b5d6888e9a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{41.76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285712} {:answer/id #uuid "7563b972-a56a-5e20-bcca-3b93dbeb33d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88.21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285874} {:answer/id #uuid "b22c1e27-5533-5369-af98-01bed62aedb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63.23}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b22c1e27-5533-5369-af98-01bed62aedb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63.23}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286418} :answer-field/id #uuid "00946ca6-d331-5035-af7f-6358bac999fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55edb4d5-3b9c-5d76-92b8-3984566f5539" :question/math-academy-id "q-19039" :question/problem "Given that $m\\cdot n=10$, find the angle between $m=⟨t,-t,3⟩$ and $n=⟨3,2,4⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, since $m\\cdot n=10$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\\cdot n & =10 \\\\ t\\cdot 3+(-t)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4 & =10 \\\\ 3t-2t+12 & =10 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =⟨(-2),-(-2),3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $m$ and $n$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{m\\cdot n}{|\\,m\\,||\\,n\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{m}_{x}{n}_{x}+{m}_{y}{n}_{y}+{m}_{z}{n}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{m}_{x}^{2}+{m}_{y}^{2}+{m}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{n}_{x}^{2}+{n}_{y}^{2}+{n}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{17}\\cdot \\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{493}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{493}})≈{63.23}^{∘}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d15acc-1672-5ec4-bb78-f3474884b897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284830} {:answer/id #uuid "48fabaf5-be8a-589c-8cf0-074c455a9240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285458} {:answer/id #uuid "63f73e2e-4004-5fc8-9825-f8337f6c2b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285697} {:answer/id #uuid "766bb2aa-4af5-5e09-aed3-a777505c1a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285891} {:answer/id #uuid "e40e7c86-1ed2-5d5e-9940-61e65ceaec5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e40e7c86-1ed2-5d5e-9940-61e65ceaec5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286873} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8570317-ecab-5ed9-a868-188d2c2ead8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9daa906-697e-5ad9-9a96-96e98679f403" :question/math-academy-id "q-1904" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ if $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+5csc⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{d}{dx}(-{x}^{2}+5csc⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-x)+5(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & =-2x-5csc⁡xcot⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the derivative and get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-2(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-5csc⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})cot⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-5\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-10\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29f3f2bf-80ee-563e-9d38-7fec626f4767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285155} {:answer/id #uuid "51eb0b49-5b85-5141-9a1b-7c05a3aa4924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{67.13}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285542} {:answer/id #uuid "7ffa284e-189c-5217-ada9-09e584526f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{87.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285966} {:answer/id #uuid "a32510c7-767d-533a-80aa-dfc214411702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88.21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286282} {:answer/id #uuid "e7187648-ecc0-524c-bb7a-ad17442ebcef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{72.34}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29f3f2bf-80ee-563e-9d38-7fec626f4767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285155} :answer-field/id #uuid "78431692-060b-5a8a-98b0-ef9f30befc89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18e3b79f-840c-5349-b289-81ab8870d68c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19040" :question/problem "Given that $g\\cdot h=8$, find the angle between $g=⟨t,t,t-1⟩$ and $h=⟨4,-2,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, since $g\\cdot h=8$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =8 \\\\ t\\cdot 4+t\\cdot (-2)+(t-1)\\cdot (-1) & =8 \\\\ 4t-2t-t+1 & =8 \\\\ t+1 & =8 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g & =⟨7,7,7-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,7,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $g$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{g\\cdot h}{|\\,g\\,||\\,h\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{g}_{x}{h}_{x}+{g}_{y}{h}_{y}+{g}_{z}{h}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{g}_{x}^{2}+{g}_{y}^{2}+{g}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{h}_{x}^{2}+{h}_{y}^{2}+{h}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{134}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}})≈{81.33}^{∘}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08847216-8695-5c58-9c55-4efd9ea37cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284855} {:answer/id #uuid "713ca5fb-8006-5933-96ce-17ac96219558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285826} {:answer/id #uuid "75c3ab8f-18e2-59e5-b409-f23279f422cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccotx-\\frac{({x}^{3}+2x)(3{x}^{2}+2)}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285882} {:answer/id #uuid "a0bb6a0e-a3e1-53de-bf1c-a588c28c1165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286254} {:answer/id #uuid "a3628ab9-5c34-5c92-bef6-1314d9e06e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08847216-8695-5c58-9c55-4efd9ea37cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284855} :answer-field/id #uuid "751d5f7c-e24c-5495-bd5f-426fdee41841" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd1d008a-84eb-52df-bb09-d41421bc5f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-19065" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=({x}^{3}+2x)arccotx.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(({x}^{3}+2x)arccotx) \\\\  & =arccotx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+2x)+({x}^{3}+2x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx) \\\\  & =arccotx\\cdot (3{x}^{2}+2)+({x}^{3}+2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c998c3-16a5-5186-a341-ea5db157e875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284935} {:answer/id #uuid "361c6acf-d3c4-566b-81c5-4427943429df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285288} {:answer/id #uuid "52f316ad-3c3e-52eb-aff0-84068ba4a2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285549} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb9929b-9ec9-53dc-8eef-e5d5f9b92e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(3{x}^{2})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285639} {:answer/id #uuid "a626cf8e-2190-59a0-ac5b-d97bc0916669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1)}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52f316ad-3c3e-52eb-aff0-84068ba4a2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285549} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5b5a09f-002f-5cfd-b2b9-fcc7e7b6ff20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "acce5149-acaa-575b-8d72-2597df12abd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-19071" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-({x}^{3})^{2}}})\\cdot (3{x}^{2})-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x})}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0810a2d0-0ce3-58a3-9628-07a5b6ebcc2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284850} {:answer/id #uuid "5624953c-3d14-5211-9d3b-b99bd07795e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285579} {:answer/id #uuid "928132bd-96e6-5295-82ca-5687c1d9b59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286118} {:answer/id #uuid "a74373f1-aca2-51a2-8b3c-f754f55d3b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{112}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286312} {:answer/id #uuid "d7340d34-1702-5e16-9dd2-b5e02a6027eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0810a2d0-0ce3-58a3-9628-07a5b6ebcc2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284850} :answer-field/id #uuid "50d04ce3-a358-500a-aed7-d670d76e14d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea49a8dd-e4b2-55bc-b471-da1f1d77c574" :question/math-academy-id "q-19107" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,1,-1)$, $B(3,-2,2)$, and $C(-1,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](images/28/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079ab0d0-3cbc-5082-b6ab-365990a42e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{93.32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284845} {:answer/id #uuid "2289598c-d338-5f6b-9292-973ab0684d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285098} {:answer/id #uuid "34289431-f128-575f-97c2-e4e6f94e3262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88.29}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285268} {:answer/id #uuid "83273044-960b-5f85-92e0-995f1a281dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52.15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285991} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cd56ba-92df-53d0-857a-cb0a2bbe1247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{67.48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2289598c-d338-5f6b-9292-973ab0684d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285098} :answer-field/id #uuid "acb00cac-bbd3-5fdd-ada8-fc80dcbf1675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "567d9479-bc13-5331-b757-cfe1cd8387a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-19119" :question/problem "Consider the points $D(1,3,2)$, $E(t,2,4)$ and $F(3,t,3).$ Find $∠EDF$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $D$, $E$, $F$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩,\\,e=⟨t,\\,2,\\,4⟩,\\,f=⟨3,\\,t,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△DEF$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠EDF=\\theta .$\n\n![](images/c9/c9cfb3e84e6f76d243125f2a09246b2a1300a0134e71359bb2b528082f064f93.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,2,\\,4⟩-⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t-1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,t,\\,3⟩-⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,t-3,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=2$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =2 \\\\ (t-1)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (t-3)+2\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 2t-2-t+3+2 & =2 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨-1-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,2⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨2,-1-3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}}{|\\overset{\\to }{DE}||\\overset{\\to }{DF}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{21}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{21}})≈{81.64}^{∘}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51f1a168-e459-5855-9f32-c7f995528292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285543} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0ca20c-6282-53b7-a446-f76828bdd080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286224} {:answer/id #uuid "b1302f72-3e46-5025-ab0e-97b643675a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286407} {:answer/id #uuid "c07b1571-e4fd-5a58-a381-73bd15f01a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286548} {:answer/id #uuid "cb5ff959-29d9-5163-867c-ef6c1827374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb5ff959-29d9-5163-867c-ef6c1827374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286643} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c576604-9cab-5f35-9107-e12da3cf2cf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b19c031-650e-5cdc-af13-3ca3ed0d48bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-19220" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,a\\,|=36$, $|\\,b\\,|=6$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={135}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$ in terms of the vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =36\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-18\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $b:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{b}{6}=\\frac{1}{6}b\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =(-18\\sqrt{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}b \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{2}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "733a21b6-530d-58ad-a226-6cac63423ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{ln⁡10}-sin⁡xlog⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285849} {:answer/id #uuid "b59cbc6b-900a-5727-b8b9-ede6d31b43fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{x}-sin⁡xlog⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286442} {:answer/id #uuid "b7de04db-df2e-5b86-833c-791e2ab5c775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{xln⁡10}+sin⁡xlog⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286464} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d4f500-323e-5311-9fac-df967ad59f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{xln⁡10}-sin⁡xlog⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286604} {:answer/id #uuid "df108f3b-d4a9-5d27-b27b-ac44d2256aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{x}-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5d4f500-323e-5311-9fac-df967ad59f73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{xln⁡10}-sin⁡xlog⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286604} :answer-field/id #uuid "87489006-c764-5370-a687-c0a258ab9b3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d56c895-83f0-5d1c-bce1-e5e5d8df4d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-1934" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=cos⁡xlog⁡x,$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=cos⁡x$ and $v(x)=log⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(cos⁡x)}^{′}log⁡x+cos⁡x{(log⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =(-sin⁡x)(log⁡x)+(cos⁡x)(\\frac{1}{xln⁡10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{cos⁡x}{xln⁡10}-sin⁡xlog⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07df5620-8117-5d74-b65a-568506c2ddda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284848} {:answer/id #uuid "4699fac1-5a8f-5b40-afed-7064158b1c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285437} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce9442e-a29f-597e-b2de-7761a1d30d17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286222} {:answer/id #uuid "a22f372f-9504-584b-bc3e-87c16eaabc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286274} {:answer/id #uuid "e584a0a9-3825-5a55-8fc4-911388ec2a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a22f372f-9504-584b-bc3e-87c16eaabc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286274} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ff436e5-f03c-513f-b406-812caeb45b91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25b26ce0-b29c-55b2-a912-d3113c434dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-19393" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/16)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/16}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287948 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d80d0e0-9bd2-5847-a397-4724c3057fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285054} {:answer/id #uuid "3747dab2-20e2-5204-ae8b-0a113e2d33ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.33\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285305} {:answer/id #uuid "730a722c-8850-546f-9ebc-6254d001cb58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285848} {:answer/id #uuid "7b67df03-e492-56d7-8841-49f60df8214b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285928} {:answer/id #uuid "9dced903-657f-5b82-b43e-657f7a6ac54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "730a722c-8850-546f-9ebc-6254d001cb58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285848} :answer-field/id #uuid "28db9891-a8b4-5ba5-bf63-10d35ddcb833" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f92df3af-103a-5ab3-9499-0ec818b5b026" :question/math-academy-id "q-19487" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}$, find the velocity of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t).$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the velocity at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =0.75\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df8b9fa-c71a-55ec-a8d2-11dd45bde6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284908} {:answer/id #uuid "5b83eb2e-77da-59bf-9250-c4d5985607be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285626} {:answer/id #uuid "94460345-d42d-5bb6-a63f-2b14d2c7b5b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.625\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286136} {:answer/id #uuid "e4847c40-c65f-5026-b4f1-6b54a618a24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286880} {:answer/id #uuid "ea1d7750-34db-55cb-94d1-d5566c6482d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea1d7750-34db-55cb-94d1-d5566c6482d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286930} :answer-field/id #uuid "f88d4908-8f9d-577d-b2cb-299f990c0866" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8470353d-eb7f-5e21-8ec9-05f72aa6f6a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-19489" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t),$ where $a(t)$ is measured in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and $t$ is measured in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4(-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t))+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(0)=\\frac{4}{5}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)+C \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+C \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 1+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t).$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =-0.8\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $0.8\\,\\text{m/s}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287952 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae5f597-51dc-537c-97d8-2213e77b66a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285163} {:answer/id #uuid "5c981f04-9a7b-5f9e-b012-5b3ed4e5537d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285636} {:answer/id #uuid "60c0e328-a8db-5493-aa2a-248624490bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285677} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fee3b0-7e49-5f47-8edd-50fc138289e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286448} {:answer/id #uuid "bbeecb8d-8395-52f9-b6fb-7671c4b447e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ae5f597-51dc-537c-97d8-2213e77b66a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285163} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5818e62-465a-5e39-9967-d2bce0bca1bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7599d445-5344-5472-bfea-dd4cab006b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-19527" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{3}^{3+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}-6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+10 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+10 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+10 \\\\  & =(x-3)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{{x}^{2}-6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{5}{(x-3)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-3)$.\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-3.\n$$\n\n \nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u$.\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $3+\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u$, and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{3+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{5}{{x}^{2}-6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{3}^{3+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =5(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "350096c6-a564-5b13-9323-1f11b8aa5aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{\\pi /4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285275} {:answer/id #uuid "356014bd-2e78-54b8-b0b0-a26c4f89ea3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285277} {:answer/id #uuid "afb947fe-8e6d-5b21-8c84-9d36b0e511e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{-\\pi /4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286390} {:answer/id #uuid "c2105640-4979-51fa-87a3-fc2d8a9feddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286564} {:answer/id #uuid "f5026c60-d19c-5056-93eb-03f4608bdbda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2105640-4979-51fa-87a3-fc2d8a9feddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286564} :answer-field/id #uuid "059711ce-e66a-51ec-8839-dd341320f202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "feb9e004-f407-5daf-8181-931953281eea" :question/math-academy-id "q-20070" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa1c1c3ae2769f45854de4f0b00fc394fccb40b40704cfd09e6eb11eee3c07af.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=3{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{e}^{2\\theta }+9{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{18{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "471b8112-fe03-5559-8fd9-7d262e3aacb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285445} {:answer/id #uuid "51beac23-bf68-50c9-952d-653cee2aa6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285540} {:answer/id #uuid "71ac35f1-a93a-56ba-81c5-2d2d400444ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285834} {:answer/id #uuid "82f17c2a-2ee4-5365-bf0f-241c55acae58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285989} {:answer/id #uuid "aa74e9c4-0cc5-5f42-a6c7-ce6192d80edf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51beac23-bf68-50c9-952d-653cee2aa6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285540} :answer-field/id #uuid "8be7a502-2728-5180-92ba-ee5a5a51b7d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe360508-b564-5f2e-8656-ff74569f459b" :question/math-academy-id "q-20214" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-3 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](images/6b/6bc5aed39e6421b8ff2416edb75dc888c8f38ae14f99b3d6e28d8e4c9302908f.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi $ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =X-2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}-2\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot (-\\frac{5\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ebdb089-b3f4-5c9d-b7a6-72e8d7a0fb70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\nM∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right],\n$$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285062} {:answer/id #uuid "478598de-5580-5d87-b084-ce12adf081bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\nM∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{array}\\right],\n$$\n$\\,x=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285447} {:answer/id #uuid "6d451244-55cd-5a96-a900-de7d2916ac34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\nM∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right],\n$$\n$\\,x=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and $y=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285793} {:answer/id #uuid "dd96eee0-cec3-575c-9ac6-6f1c4fbaca49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\nM∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right],\n$$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286805} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ce9517-b274-5d83-a6ad-5f9bd48e8700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\nM∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right],\n$$\n$\\,x=\\frac{20}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd96eee0-cec3-575c-9ac6-6f1c4fbaca49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\nM∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right],\n$$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286805} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1c4de6-304d-5776-887d-6ed5bb7bf942" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f7d8f30-0a86-56e1-866a-295695eb3958" :question/math-academy-id "q-20459" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=\\frac{10}{3} \\\\ y &=-\\frac{5}{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{5}{3})=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,x=\\frac{10}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$"}]
